---
import LegalPage from "../components/shared/legal-page/index.astro";

const title = "Andesine Support";
const description = "Get help with Andesine.";
---

<LegalPage title={title} description={description} path="/support/">
  <h1>Andesine Support</h1>
  <p>
    Email us at <a href="mailto:support@andesine.app">support@andesine.app</a>. We usually reply
    within two business days.
  </p>
  <h3>Before you write</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>
      Read the <a href="/docs">documentation</a>. It explains setup, the editor, publishing, the
      API, the CLI, MCP, and extensions.
    </li>
    <li>
      Ask questions and share ideas in
      <a href="https://github.com/vriteio/andesine/discussions">GitHub Discussions</a>.
    </li>
    <li>
      Report bugs in <a href="https://github.com/vriteio/andesine/issues">GitHub Issues</a>.
    </li>
  </ul>
  <h3>What to include</h3>
  <ul>
    <li>The email address of your Andesine account.</li>
    <li>The workspace name, if the problem is about a workspace.</li>
    <li>The steps that cause the problem, and what you expected to see.</li>
  </ul>
  <p>Do not send passwords, API keys, or other secrets.</p>
  <h3>Billing, privacy, and account requests</h3>
  <p>
    Email <a href="mailto:support@andesine.app">support@andesine.app</a> from the email address of your
    account. This includes questions about invoices, data access or deletion requests, and connected apps.
    The <a href="/privacy">privacy policy</a> describes your data rights.
  </p>
  <h3>Security issues</h3>
  <p>
    Do not report security issues in public. Email
    <a href="mailto:support@andesine.app">support@andesine.app</a> with the subject "Security" and the
    steps to reproduce the issue.
  </p>
</LegalPage>
